WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:02.639
Fully autonomous flight may seem easy.

00:00:02.639 --> 00:00:08.130
You don’t need to stick to roads and have
much more space to maneuver and avoid obstacles,

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:11.720
but detecting other aircraft can be hard.

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:18.410
Even in the US 90% of low altitude flights
don’t require transponders that would allow

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:21.770
drones to detect other aircraft.

00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:27.880
Drones need cheap and low weight sensors that
can see through fog and clouds with 360 degrees

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:29.710
of spherical sight.

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:35.359
Zipline had a batty idea to do this with cheap
off the shelf sensors.

00:00:35.359 --> 00:00:36.569
Microphones.

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:43.139
Zipline has created a reliable system that
can pinpoint aircraft locations in 3D space

00:00:43.139 --> 00:00:48.629
using these 8 microphones using signal processing
algorithms.

00:00:48.629 --> 00:00:55.039
Allowing their drones to automatically detect
and avoid aircraft, bringing us one step closer

00:00:55.039 --> 00:00:58.420
to safe drone integration in our airspace.

